From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 21:39:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: disable automatic onboarding

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Start local jcode sessions without an automatic onboarding flow.
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 1010-personal-feature-remove-sponsored-integration-discovery.patch

Patch intent:
Disable startup and post-login entry points for the guided onboarding flow and
prevent ordinary empty sessions from rendering its welcome layout. Keep the
existing manual login and provider configuration surfaces available.

Why it exists:
A fresh local session must open directly into the ordinary usable session state
without a welcome wizard, setup pitch, or forced model/login walkthrough.

Upstream integration points:
The patch changes TUI onboarding flow control, empty-session welcome activation,
and their startup regression tests. It leaves the manual onboarding code
reachable only through explicit preview, simulation, or development paths
until a later cleanup patch removes it.

Update guidance:
Do not restore automatic onboarding or its welcome layout from ordinary startup
or login callbacks. Preserve manual provider login and direct session usability
on a fresh launch.

Validation:
scripts/cargo_exec.sh check -p jcode-tui
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-tui startup_check_never_starts_automatic_onboarding --lib
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-tui fresh_empty_session_does_not_render_onboarding_welcome --lib
